Short Answer
In 1-2 sentences, explain the difference between using an MLP for regression and using an MLP for classification.

ANSWER = MLPs used for regression output a single continuous value with a linear activation and are trained using Mean Squared Error.  
MLPs used for classification output probabilities for each class using a softmax activation and are trained with Cross-Entropy loss.

